## Dicas da tela de carregamento (gerado por tools/gerar-dicas.mjs)
beginnerTips.1=Your ship crashed, but the hull is a shelter: at night, stay inside the plane or somewhere lit.
beginnerTips.2=Open the Logbook: each quest teaches the next step and gives a reward.
beginnerTips.3=The Water Condenser in the plane's chest pulls water from the air. Place it on day one.
beginnerTips.4=There is almost no ore in sight: with a hammer, stone becomes gravel, gravel becomes sand and sand becomes dust.
beginnerTips.5=In the Sieve, gravel, sand and dust drop ores, seeds and more.
beginnerTips.6=Under the midday sun your body heats up: stay in the shade and drink water.
beginnerTips.7=Salt or dirty water is not safe to drink: boil it in a furnace, on a campfire or in a cauldron over fire.
beginnerTips.8=By day monsters bury themselves in the sand. At night they come back.
beginnerTips.9=No animals live here: they arrive in the cargo capsules that fall from the sky.
beginnerTips.10=The Catalog shows how to make any item and where it is used.
beginnerTips.11=Every crafting recipe shows up in the inventory recipe book.
beginnerTips.12=Lost? The Plane Compass shows which way and how far the Ship Console is.
midgameTips.1=Your ship crashed, but the hull is a shelter: at night, stay inside the plane or somewhere lit.
midgameTips.2=Open the Logbook: each quest teaches the next step and gives a reward.
midgameTips.3=The Water Condenser in the plane's chest pulls water from the air. Place it on day one.
midgameTips.4=There is almost no ore in sight: with a hammer, stone becomes gravel, gravel becomes sand and sand becomes dust.
midgameTips.5=In the Sieve, gravel, sand and dust drop ores, seeds and more.
midgameTips.6=Under the midday sun your body heats up: stay in the shade and drink water.
midgameTips.7=Salt or dirty water is not safe to drink: boil it in a furnace, on a campfire or in a cauldron over fire.
midgameTips.8=By day monsters bury themselves in the sand. At night they come back.
midgameTips.9=No animals live here: they arrive in the cargo capsules that fall from the sky.
midgameTips.10=The Catalog shows how to make any item and where it is used.
midgameTips.11=Every crafting recipe shows up in the inventory recipe book.
midgameTips.12=Lost? The Plane Compass shows which way and how far the Ship Console is.
midgameTips.13=Every 10 nights a horde comes, with a warning at dusk. Get your defenses ready.
midgameTips.14=Sandstorms bring the Sand Golem.
midgameTips.15=When you are safe, the Sleeping Bag skips the night.
midgameTips.16=The Camel Pack carries water with you on long trips.
midgameTips.17=Eating the same thing gets old: the game remembers your last 12 meals. Vary your diet.
midgameTips.18=Date palm saplings come from sifting sand, and they grow bunches of dates.
midgameTips.19=The Drying Rack dries raw meat into Beef Jerky.
midgameTips.20=Abandoned cities have a radio signal: they hold parts that cannot be crafted.
midgameTips.21=Saw a meteor fall? The coordinates show in chat. Meteorite rock drops ores and sometimes diamond.
midgameTips.22=Power first: a generator, solar panels, batteries and cables open the way to machines.
midgameTips.23=Machines multiply ores: one ore can yield more than one ingot.
midgameTips.24=Tinkers' tools can be repaired and gain modifiers at the Tool Station.
midgameTips.25=Oil lies deep below the sand. The Pump extracts it and the Refinery makes fuel.
midgameTips.26=Hold the Hang Glider while falling to glide forward. Sneak to close it.
midgameTips.27=Two Elevators, one above the other: jump to go up, sneak to go down.
midgameTips.28=When you die, your items go into a Grave on the spot, with the coordinates in chat.
midgameTips.29=Storage Barrels hold a lot of a single item.
midgameTips.30=In an AE network all items are stored together and the terminal finds any of them.
midgameTips.31=There is no air on the Moon: wear the Oxygen Mask and Oxygen Gear and carry full tanks. A light tank lasts almost 7 minutes.
midgameTips.32=The rocket lands on the Moon, but only lifts off from a 3×3 pad: bring 9 pads, a fuel loader and power.
midgameTips.33=The Mekanism paxel is a pickaxe, an axe and a shovel in one tool.
midgameTips.34=The Mekanism Wind Generator makes more power the higher it is.
midgameTips.35=Two Ender IO Travel Anchors within 96 blocks: tap one to travel to the other.
midgameTips.36=The Nether portal won't light here: a hammer turns netherrack into Nether Gravel, and sifting it gives quartz and even netherite.
midgameTips.37=Four systems burned in the crash: hull, flight computer, fuel and engine.
midgameTips.38=The Ship Console in the plane's cockpit repairs each system once you have the parts.
midgameTips.39=With all four systems repaired, the Jump Coil is still missing: the Jump Core is in the lunar research base.
midgameTips.40=On the Moon, the Plane Compass points to the research base signal.
midgameTips.41=No one is coming for you. The only way out is to repair the ship and take off.
midgameTips.42=Each mod has a chapter in the Logbook. Follow it to the end to go home.
